WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:07.200
We have seen that the opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.100
add up to 180 degrees.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.340
A quadrilateral is cyclic

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.840
when a circle  passes through all its four vertices.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.380
Of course it's an important property

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.120
but we need to prove this result.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.380
We are given that quadrilateral ABCD is cyclic.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:27.860
And we have to prove

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:32.300
that it's opposite angles add up to 180 degrees.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.860
This would mean

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.640
angle A plus angle C equals 180 degrees.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:43.500
And angle B plus angle D equals 180 degrees.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.680
The figure we have is absolutely blank.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.620
Nothing is given to us about the sides or the angles.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.260
The only thing we do know

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.500
is that all the four vertices ABC and D lie on the circle.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.700
Since the figure tells us nothing,

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.380
let's try and analyze what we have to prove first.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.620
We have to prove that the sum of angles is 180 degrees.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.220
Looking at this 180 degrees,

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.780
we would probably have to form a triangle somewhere in the figure

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.420
and use the sum of Interior angles concept.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.960
If we join any one diagonal,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.140
we get two triangles.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:28.140
But these two triangles also don't tell us anything.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.120
So in our construction

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.600
let us join both the diagonals AC and BD.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.500
AC and BD.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.000
That gives us four triangles,

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.160
but we won't use all of them.

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:43.800
More than triangles,

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.580
what this gives us is angles in the same segment.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.380
We will understand it in the proof.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.280
There are four chords AB, BC, CD

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.320
and DA in this circle

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:00.320
and each one divides the circle into two segments.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.840
Now understand this really well,

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.440
the colored region is a major segment formed by chord AB.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.920
And angle ACB and angle ADB lie in that segment.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:16.560
Since angles formed in the same segment are equal,

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:22.080
we can say that angle ACB is equal to angle ADB.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.200
Now look at this blue region.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.160
It is a major segment formed

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.360
by chord BC and it contains two angles,

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:33.000
angle BAC and angle BDC.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:38.700
So, we can say that angle BAC is equal to angle BDC.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:43.000
Both these pairs are angles formed in the same segment.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:44.820
Look at the figure now.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.760
If we add angle ADB and angle BDC,

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.660
we will get angle ADC which is actually angle D.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.060
So if we add the right hand sides of these two equations,

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.300
we get angle D

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.820
But we can't just add the right hand sides,

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:05.060
we will have to add the left hand sides too.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.260
Adding these two equations,

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.060
We get angle ACB plus angle BAC

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.380
equals angle D.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.880
It gets even more interesting.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.820
Since we are looking for 180 degrees,

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.840
we have to look for sum of angles of a triangle.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.080
Look at the left-hand side.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.260
It's angle ACB plus angle BAC.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:34.020
This is angle ACB and this is angle BAC.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.380
If we look at triangle ACB

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.500
the only angle left out is angle ABC.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.880
If we add angle ABC to the left hand side,

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.980
we will get the sum of all the angles of a triangle ACB.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:52.520
When, we add angle ABC to the left hand side,

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.720
we also have to add it to the right hand side.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.900
So, we add angle ABC to both the sides.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:04.180
This was one of the most crucial steps in this proof.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.440
You will realize that angle ABC

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:13.180
is the only angle that is left out and we are looking for 180 degrees.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:17.720
With this step, we get angle ABC plus angle BAC

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:24.200
plus angle ABC equal to angle D plus angle ABC.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.400
This left hand side as we saw

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.960
is the sum of all angles of a triangle ACB

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.020
which equals 180 degrees.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.400
The equation we get, is

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:40.440
180 degrees equals angle D plus angle ABC.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.240
we're almost there!

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:46.860
Angle ABC is actually angle B of the quadrilateral.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:53.520
So, we can say that angle D plus angle B equal to 180 degrees.

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.860
So we proved one part.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.940
What about the second part?

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.280
The proof of the second part is very simple.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.600
We know that the sum of all angles of a quadrilateral

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.360
is 360 degrees.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.920
Angle A plus angle B plus angle C

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:15.520
plus angle D equals 360 degrees.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:19.060
And out of these four, we know that B and D

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.920
add up to 180 degrees.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:26.700
So, we get angle A plus angle C plus 180 degrees

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.560
equal to 360 degrees.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:34.400
We just replaced B plus D with 180 degrees.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.640
Transposing 180 degrees to the right hand side,

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:43.620
we get angle A plus angle C equal to 180 degrees.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.520
This was bit long, but remember, the most important part of the proof

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:51.080
was to look for equal angles in a segment,

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:56.460
and adding an angle to get the sum of all angles of one triangle.

